      "math_academy_id": "e-3979",
      "problem": "The equation $\\log_{6}{1} = 0$ is equivalent to $b^0 = 1.$ What is the value of $b?$",
      "worked_solution": "The logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n$\\log_{b}{a} = x$ is equivalent to $a = b^x$\n\nIf we compare $\\log_{6}{1} = 0$ with $\\log_{b}{a} = x,$ we get $a = 1,$ $b = 6,$ and $x = 0.$\n\nTherefore, the given equation is equivalent to $6^0 = 1.$ Consequently, $b = 6.$",
